   00001| //! Whole-line operations a request states by position, adjacency or exchange.
   00002| //!
   00003| //! PR #1188 dogfooding: `Delete lines 266-267 from f.lino.` only read the
   00004| //! file (T30), `Insert the line '…' after line 12 in f.lino.` planned nothing
   00005| //! (T33), `delete the line 'A' and the 'B' line directly above it` was routed
   00006| //! to a whole-file write of a fragment (T29), `Move the line 'x' to the top
   00007| //! of f` duplicated the line and `Swap the lines 'a' and 'b' in f` planned
   00008| //! nothing. Each is now a computed change over the file's lines (read,
   00009| //! compute, the smallest unique edit, the digest check, the seeded sentence),
   00010| //! run by [`super::workspace_computed_change`]. Every word that carries the
   00011| //! operation is seeded (`numbered_line_noun`, `numbered_line_lead`,
   00012| //! `line_range_connector`, `line_adjacent_above`, `line_adjacent_below`,
   00013| //! `line_move_action`, `line_swap_action`) in every registered language.
   00014| //! Mirrors `js/agentic/workspace_line_operation.mjs`.
